  "notes": "Soul-rooted torch pop with live-room drums, and one of the fully documented entries in this section — key, tempo, range, voicing family, chord progressions and production method are all sourced. The backbeat is straight but the *instrument* is not a kit: \"martial beats — a four-square kick with hand-claps and foot-stomps on the backbeat, played rather than programmed, in a live room; the kit is often absent from verse one entirely and enters as the structural event.\" So the kick anchors all four beats, the snare stack is `clap` alone with a wide human offset and a large room tail, `hihat.continuous` is false at `fillDensity` 0.05 with the roll vocabulary off, and the perc lanes are `tom` and `tambourine` at `downbeat`. The humanize block is a played one. Harmony is transcribed as degrees from the entry's own roman numerals — \"VI—VII—v … V\" and \"i—VII—VImaj7—VII\" — with the maj7 in `extensions` and a `borrowed` V because the source names both v and V. The documented open-fifth bottom (\"the harmonic bottom is frequently open fifths rather than full chords: C5—G5—B♭5—G5—B♭5, i.e. i5—v5—VII5\") is why `triad` sits at 0.84 and the voicing is open and wide: a fifth is what is left when the third is gone. Melody register is the documented B♭3—D5 contralto span, \"a compact 10th and pushed at the top\"; \"wide-interval, chest-driven and rhythmically front-loaded\" is the leap share and the arch contour. The counter is the \"massed backing-vocal chant\". ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize numbers and the perc gain. `bpm.mode` 105 is the entry's own stated flagship tempo, not an inference.",
